{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The threshold test under POL-RD-01 is governed by the trace figure, and the trace says this trip was driven 11.18 km against a booked optimal of 8.2 km. The derived excess is 2.98 km, or 36.34% of optimal, so both limbs of the POL-RD-01 gate are passed (more than 0.8 km absolute and more than 20% of optimal) and a route deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own telemetry. I rely on gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 11.18 km, not on trip_record.actual_distance_km of 11.2 km, as POL-RD-01 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00103", "EV-TRIP-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08(a) is discharged: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-00103 and agree on the trip's timing, the trace running from 08:07:20 to 08:36:20 on 14 July 2026 against a trip_record that starts at 08:07:20 and ends at 08:36:20. The three artifacts describe the same trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00103", "EV-GPS-00103", "EV-FARE-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "first_fix_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean for policy purposes and no escalation under POL-RD-10(3) is available to the driver: coverage is 100%, there are 175 fixes at a 10 second sampling interval against an expected interval of 10 seconds, the gaps array is empty and max_gap_sec is 0.0. None of limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07 fires, so no independent corroboration is required and the trace may be used directly.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not need corroboration beyond the trace to bring this claim: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the POL-RD-08 rider-profile sub-limb (4 or more claims with 1 or fewer substantiated) does not engage and no extra independent source is required for an excess of this size.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The diversion itself is genuine and the rider does not contest the driver's side of the distance-and-time question: LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20260714-031 closes Braddell Road (towards Serangoon) between Lorong 1 Toa Payoh and Bishan Rd from 05:30 to 12:00, that is the very arterial the routing engine's stored optimal route uses, and the advisory's window overlaps the trip window. All three limbs of POL-RD-03 are met, so the measured excess is exonerated on distance and time. That exoneration is, however, the predicate for the pass-through correction claimed below, not a reason to leave the rider paying the CTE gantries.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00103-01", "EV-TRIP-00103", "EV-GPS-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.justified_excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the deviation is exonerated as an EXTERNAL EVENT under POL-RD-03, POL-RD-09(2) applies on its own terms: the distance and time charges stand, but the off-route ERP charges are still refunded to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction, capped at SGD 12.00 per trip. The off-route ERP actually charged is $4.00, so the full $4.00 is due and the cap is nowhere near binding. The rider did not cause the closure and should not bear its gantry cost.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00103", "EV-ADVIS-00103-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Both charged gantries are on the record as off the optimal route: CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) at $3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) at $1.00 each carry on_optimal_route false, and the trip_record's optimal_route_erp_sgd is 0.00, matching the rider's account that the route she booked carries no gantry at all. The whole $4.00 was incurred solely by the CTE diversion and none of it is a charge the optimal route would have attracted.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00103", "EV-TRIP-00103", "EV-GPS-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.on_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot convert this into a rider-caused detour and so cannot shut off the ERP correction through POL-RD-09(3). POL-RD-04(a) requires the instruction to come from the rider; the only message naming a route came from the DRIVER ('braddell close today, i take CTE ah', sent 08:12:30), and the rider's single reply 'ok' at 08:12:58 is a bare acknowledgement of a decision the driver had already announced, not an instruction identifying a place or road to act on, with waypoint_hint null on the record. POL-RD-04 is unavailable, and the pass-through refund under POL-RD-09(2) remains payable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00103", "EV-FARE-00103"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the fare breakdown's own closure arithmetic the correction is at least as large: running the POL-RD-02 recomputation against the closure-adjusted optimal of 11.18 km and 28.6 minutes gives a recomputed fare of $20.993 against a charged total of $25.12, a differential of $4.127, which rounds UP to $4.15 under the fare_model rounding rule. If the tribunal takes that route rather than the POL-RD-09(2) standalone correction, the amount payable is $4.15; and under POL-RD-09(1) the $4.00 of ERP is in that case already comprehended inside the figure and must not be added on top of it. The two routes to the correction are alternatives, not cumulative.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00103", "EV-TRIP-00103", "EV-ADVIS-00103-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the essential facts, so this can be brief. The trip was driven 11.18 km along the GPS trace against a booked optimal of 8.2 km — an excess of 2.98 km, or 36.34% — which passes the POL-RD-01 threshold (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%). LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20260714-031 closed Braddell Road (towards Serangoon) between Lorong 1 Toa Payoh and Bishan Rd from 05:30 to 12:00 on 14 July 2026, which is the arterial the booked optimal route uses, and the driver's trace leaves that corridor at the Lorong 1 Toa Payoh slip inside the closed geometry before rejoining it. That is a full exoneration under POL-RD-03: the justified excess is the lesser of the measured 2.98 km and the cap of 4.12 km (1.30 x (10.6 - 8.2) + 1.0 tolerance), so the whole excess is justified, the closure-adjusted optimal is 11.18 km, and no unexcused excess remains. POL-RD-02 therefore does not run and the distance and time charges stand. What the rider did not cause is the ERP. Both charged gantries — CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) at $3.00 and CTE (Moulmein Rd towards City) at $1.00 — are marked on_optimal_route false, and the trip record's optimal_route_erp_sgd is $0.00, so the booked route carries no gantry at all. POL-RD-09(2) returns off-route ERP to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction where the deviation is an external event, capped at $12.00. The off-route ERP is $4.00, so I order $4.00 refunded. On the two points the briefs dispute: the rider's alternative figure of $4.15 depends on running POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal, and that route is not open, because POL-RD-03 fully excuses the deviation and POL-RD-02 by its own terms applies only where no exculpatory clause fully excuses it; had it run, POL-RD-09(1) would have comprehended the $4.00 ERP inside it rather than added to it, so the two figures were never cumulative. The driver is right that no billing-integrity referral is due: both gantries are matched to the trace (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 40.25 m away, well inside the 250 m radius), so there is no phantom line and POL-RD-09(4) is not engaged. POL-RD-04 gives the driver nothing either way — the only route message came from the driver, the rider's 'ok' is an acknowledgement rather than an instruction naming a place or road, and waypoint_hint is null — so there is no rider-caused detour to shut off the ERP correction, and no shortfall between billed and traced distance to support driver compensation. No POL-RD-06 pattern arises (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 553 completed trips), so there is no conduct referral and no FULL_REFUND uplift, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires. Figures used: charged_total $25.12; optimal_route_erp_sgd $0.00; off-route ERP $4.00 ($3.00 + $1.00); pass-through cap $12.00; trace distance 11.18 km; booked optimal 8.2 km; excess 2.98 km / 36.34%; justified-excess cap 4.12 km. Refund $4.00, rounded up to the nearest $0.05."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
